{
    "background_story": "Zion was a music enthusiast who spent most of his teenage years perfecting his DJ skills. He was particularly fascinated by the art of sound design and the impact of low-frequency bass on a crowd. Zion's friends affectionately called him the 'Subwoofer King' due to his ability to craft sets that would rattle the very foundations of the club. His love for deep, rumbling basslines led him to build his own custom subwoofer system, which quickly gained attention from local promoters. Before long, Zion was in high demand, bringing his unique sound to festivals and concerts across the country. His music was a testament to the power of the subwoofer, capable of moving both bodies and emotions.",
